{"surface":"மணியின்","parts":[{"text":"மணி","lemma":"மணி","gloss":"sapphire / gem"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"இன்","gloss":"like"}],"gloss":"like a sapphire"},{"surface":"தோன்றும்","parts":[{"text":"தோன்று","lemma":"தோன்று","gloss":"appear"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"உம்","gloss":"habitual relative participle"}],"gloss":"appears"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"தண்ணறும்","parts":[{"text":"தண்","lemma":"தண்","gloss":"cool"},{"text":"நறும்","lemma":"நறுமை","gloss":"fragrant"}],"gloss":"cool and fragrant"},{"surface":"துறுகல்","parts":[{"text":"துறு","lemma":"துறு","gloss":"thick / dense"},{"text":"கல்","lemma":"கல்","gloss":"stone / boulder"}],"gloss":"thick boulder"},{"surface":"ஓங்கிய","parts":[{"text":"ஓங்கு","lemma":"ஓங்கு","gloss":"rise high"},{"text":"இய","lemma":"இய","gloss":"past relative participle"}],"gloss":"high / lofty"},{"surface":"மலையே","parts":[{"text":"மலை","lemma":"மலை","gloss":"mountain"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"the mountain indeed"}]}],"literal":"Even if the cruel ones do not bestow grace, oh, / may your shoulders with forearms where bangles shine obtain beauty! / Look there, O friend, it has come indeed! / Because the great rain of drizzle has begun, in his country, / like a waterfall cascading joyfully with the clamor of playmates, / appearing like a washed sapphire, / the mountain with cool, fragrant, thick boulders rising high!","translation":"Even if that cruel man does not show us grace, O friend, may your shoulders, adorned with forearms where bangles shine, regain their beauty! Look there! The great, dark rain clouds have begun to pour. In his country, the high mountain with its cool, fragrant, thick boulders now appears like a polished sapphire, washed by the joyfully cascading waterfall that sounds like the clamorous play of young girls.","modern":"தோழி! கொடியவராகிய நம் தலைவர் நமக்கு அருள் செய்யாவிட்டாலும், வளையல்கள் விளங்கும் உன்னுடைய முன்கைகளை உடைய தோள்கள் அழகு பெறட்டும். அங்கே பார்! மேகங்கள் மழை பொழியத் தொடங்கியதால், அவருடைய நாட்டில், தோழியர் கூட்டத்தின் ஆரவாரத்தோடு விரும்பி இறங்கும் அருவியைப் போல, கழுவப்பட்ட நீலமணி போலத் தோன்றும் குளிர்ந்த நறுமணமுள்ள பாறைகள் உயர்ந்த மலையை பார்!","explanation":"In this poem, the friend (தோழி) is comforting the heroine (தலைவி) who is grieving the delay of her lover's return. The heroine's shoulders have grown thin, causing her bangles to slip, which is a classic sign of pining. The friend points to the sky and the distant hills of the hero's land, showing that the monsoon rains have finally arrived. She compares the cascading waterfalls on his mountain to the noisy, joyful play of young girls, and the wet rocks to polished sapphires. This beautiful sight of the rain-washed mountain serves as a reassuring sign that the hero will return soon, restoring the heroine's beauty.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}